# Milestone: M3
# Covers: ',' and '&' compile successfully at M3 but require urbi_step driver
# (urbi_strand_create-allocated strand with an entry_closure) to run. The
# uvm_run REPL path uses a stack-local transient strand with no entry_closure;
# these opcodes produce a runtime TypeError in that context. The chk runner
# uses the REPL (uvm_run path), so we expect TypeError at runtime, not emit
# error. Real concurrent execution is tested via unit tests (test_fork.c).

1 , 2
[00000001] !!! TypeError: OP_FORK_DETACH: `,` requires urbi_step driver (uvm_run transient strand)

1 & 2
[00000002] !!! TypeError: OP_FORK_JOIN: `&` requires urbi_step driver (uvm_run transient strand)
